      "updated": 1772169105710,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* what is recursion?\n=> Recursion is a technique where a function calls itself to solve a problem by breaking it into smaller subproblems.\n\nEvery recursive function must have:\n1. Base Case → stopping condition\n2. Recursive Call → function calling itself\n3. Progress toward base case",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* what is recursion?\n=> Recursion is a technique where a function calls itself to solve a problem by breaking it into smaller subproblems.\n\nEvery recursive function must have:\n1. Base Case → stopping condition\n2. Recursive Call → function calling itself\n3. Progress toward base case",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b2zWOhHPF5YB7h80uhxgg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 442,
      "width": 531.49951171875,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1576090832,
      "version": 63,
      "versionNonce": 1793701424,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772169308911,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* phase of recursion\n=> Recursion has ONLY ONE function but TWO phases\n\n1. Call Phase (Going DOWN)\n    Happens before the recursive call\n    Stack keeps growing\n    Function keeps calling itself\n\n2. Return Phase (Coming UP)\n    Happens after the recursive call\n    Stack starts unwinding\n    Code executes while returning\n\nGolden Rule\n\nCode before recursive call runs while GOING DOWN\nCode after recursive call runs while COMING UP",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* phase of recursion\n=> Recursion has ONLY ONE function but TWO phases\n\n1. Call Phase (Going DOWN)\n    Happens before the recursive call\n    Stack keeps growing\n    Function keeps calling itself\n\n2. Return Phase (Coming UP)\n    Happens after the recursive call\n    Stack starts unwinding\n    Code executes while returning\n\nGolden Rule\n\nCode before recursive call runs while GOING DOWN\nCode after recursive call runs while COMING UP",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Pm7pFYbrDtXoefyrwElWS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 346,
      "y": 903.5763125419617,
      "width": 400.7996520996094,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 688201264,
      "version": 29,
      "versionNonce": 875985616,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772169504100,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Example Showing Both Phases\n\nfunction demo(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n\n    console.log(\"DOWN:\", n); // going down\n    demo(n - 1);\n    console.log(\"UP:\", n);   // coming up\n}\n\ndemo(3);\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Example Showing Both Phases\n\nfunction demo(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n\n    console.log(\"DOWN:\", n); // going down\n    demo(n - 1);\n    console.log(\"UP:\", n);   // coming up\n}\n\ndemo(3);\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
