      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772169519721,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Types of Recursion\n1 Direct Recursion\n\nA function calls itself directly.\n\nfunction direct(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    direct(n - 1);\n}\n\n2 Indirect Recursion\n\nA function calls another function, which then calls the first function.\n\nfunction A(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    B(n - 1);\n}\n\nfunction B(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    A(n - 1);\n}\n\n3 Tail Recursion\n\nRecursive call is the last statement in the function.\n\nfunction tail(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    return tail(n - 1);\n}\n\nNo code after recursive call\nEasier to optimize (in some languages)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Types of Recursion\n1 Direct Recursion\n\nA function calls itself directly.\n\nfunction direct(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    direct(n - 1);\n}\n\n2 Indirect Recursion\n\nA function calls another function, which then calls the first function.\n\nfunction A(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    B(n - 1);\n}\n\nfunction B(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    A(n - 1);\n}\n\n3 Tail Recursion\n\nRecursive call is the last statement in the function.\n\nfunction tail(n) {\n    if (n === 0) return;\n    return tail(n - 1);\n}\n\nNo code after recursive call\nEasier to optimize (in some languages)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
