      "versionNonce": 1091850741,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1772176125751,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " REVERSE ARRAY USING RECURSION - DRY RUN WITH ASCII DIAGRAMS\n \n Example: reverseArray([1,2,3], [], 2)\n \n CALL STACK VISUALIZATION:\n ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n │ Step 1: reverseArray([1,2,3], [], 2)    │\n │ ind=2, push(arr[2])=push(3)             │\n │ revArr = [3], RECURSE → ind=1           │\n ├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n │ Step 2: reverseArray([1,2,3], [3], 1)   │\n │ ind=1, push(arr[1])=push(2)             │\n │ revArr = [3,2], RECURSE → ind=0         │\n ├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n │ Step 3: reverseArray([1,2,3], [3,2], 0) │\n │ ind=0 ← BASE CASE HIT!                  │\n │ push(arr[0])=push(1)                    │\n │ revArr = [3,2,1], RETURN                │\n └─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n \n ARRAY STATE PROGRESSION:\n Step | ind | Action            | revArr    | Status\n -----|-----|-------------------|-----------|--------\n 1    | 2   | push(arr[2])=3    | [3]       | ↓ Recurse\n 2    | 1   | push(arr[1])=2    | [3,2]     | ↓ Recurse\n 3    | 0   | push(arr[0])=1    | [3,2,1]   | BASE CASE\n -----|-----|-------------------|-----------|--------\n                                 Result: [3,2,1] ✓",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " REVERSE ARRAY USING RECURSION - DRY RUN WITH ASCII DIAGRAMS\n \n Example: reverseArray([1,2,3], [], 2)\n \n CALL STACK VISUALIZATION:\n ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n │ Step 1: reverseArray([1,2,3], [], 2)    │\n │ ind=2, push(arr[2])=push(3)             │\n │ revArr = [3], RECURSE → ind=1           │\n ├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n │ Step 2: reverseArray([1,2,3], [3], 1)   │\n │ ind=1, push(arr[1])=push(2)             │\n │ revArr = [3,2], RECURSE → ind=0         │\n ├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n │ Step 3: reverseArray([1,2,3], [3,2], 0) │\n │ ind=0 ← BASE CASE HIT!                  │\n │ push(arr[0])=push(1)                    │\n │ revArr = [3,2,1], RETURN                │\n └─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n \n ARRAY STATE PROGRESSION:\n Step | ind | Action            | revArr    | Status\n -----|-----|-------------------|-----------|--------\n 1    | 2   | push(arr[2])=3    | [3]       | ↓ Recurse\n 2    | 1   | push(arr[1])=2    | [3,2]     | ↓ Recurse\n 3    | 0   | push(arr[0])=1    | [3,2,1]   | BASE CASE\n -----|-----|-------------------|-----------|--------\n                                 Result: [3,2,1] ✓",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
